\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 11-27 BITCOIN: BTC, ETHEREUM: ETH, SOLANA: SOL, DOGWIFHAT: WIF, RIPPLE: XRP, SEI: SEI, FANTOM: FTM\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 3,015 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 November 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Market Correction Deepens }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloodbath As $581M In Derivatives Liquidated }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump Plans To Hand Over Crypto Oversight to CFTC }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) Price Analysis }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple (XRP) Price Analysis }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEI (SEI) Price Analysis }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fantom (FTM) Price Analysis }}}\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency market faces an absolute bloodbath, with Bitcoin (BTC) sliding toward the $90,000 mark as the ongoing price correction deepens amid rising liquidations and profit-taking.\par \par \uc2 BTC is down over 2% in the past 24 hours and had dipped to a low of $90,796 before recovering. The cryptocurrency is currently trading around the $92,600 price level, with \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment on the rise. The global crypto market cap also took a pummeling and is down by 2.30% at $3.19 trillion. The dip has left BTC traders reeling, with several million in long positions wiped out. Trading volume has also seen a substantial dip of almost 9%.\par \par \uc2 Almost all cryptocurrencies registered substantial declines as a deep correction took hold, dragging the market into the red. Ethereum (ETH) slipped below $3,400 and is currently down 1% over the past 24 hours. \uc2 Solana\uc2  (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ) is also in the red, with buyers struggling to keep it above $230. Ripple (XRP) has seen a substantial decline of almost 4% and is trading at $1.39. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/DOGE-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) }}}\uc2 , which saw a stunning post-election rally, also finds itself in the red, with the price down almost 3%. Other altcoins that registered substantial drops include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/XLM-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stellar (XLM) }}}\uc2 , Polkadot (DOT), Internet Computer (\uc2 ICP\uc2 ), and Cronos (CRO).\par \par \uc2 Crypto Market Correction Deepens\par \par \uc2 The crypto market came under significant pressure as prices plummeted after a buoyant post-election phase. Markets hit a five-day low as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/11/crypto-price-analysis-11-26-bitcoin-btc-ethereum-eth-solana-sol-chainlink-link-aptos-apt-injective-inj-optimism-op"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) }}}\uc2  dropped as low as $90,796, driven by a selloff in safe-haven assets as markets hope for de-escalating tensions between Israel and Lebanon. Additionally, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariff threats are playing against stock indices and weighing on equities. The Crypto Fear and Greed Index fell to 79. While this is firmly in extreme greed, it is the lowest level in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 BTC\u8217\'20\'19s drop to a low of $90,786 deepend the correction significantly, with prices dropping for the fourth consecutive day. BTC attempted to reclaim $99,000 late on Monday, but sellers countered, leading to more selling. If BTC continues dropping and goes below $90,000, we can expect a drop to $85,000 or as low as $80,000.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, data from \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  revealed global crypto fund investments reached an all-time high of $3.12 billion, following inflows worth $2.193 billion the week prior. Investments in BTC registered an increase of $3.07 billion, while ETH investments grew $3 million, \uc2 SOL\uc2  by $16 million, and XRP by $15 million. According to FalconX, the relative dominance of \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  orders in the BTC market had weakened, and growth momentum is not being supported by new buying interest.\par \par \uc2 Bloodbath As $581M In Derivatives Liquidated\par \par \uc2 The crypto market has witnessed a bloodbath in the past 24-48 hours as BTC plummeted towards a low of $90,700, a significant 3% drop compared to the previous day and a 1% decline over the past week. However, despite this substantial correction, BTC is up almost 37% over the past month. BTC\u8217\'20\'19s recent downturn caused significant liquidations in crypto derivatives, with a total of $581 million in positions wiped out. BTC long positions accounted for $113 million of liquidations, while ETH longs accounted for $77 million.\par \par \uc2 BTC and the crypto market\u8217\'20\'19s latest drop is another example of how it remains prone to significant shifts in sentiment. As institutional and retail players react to such shifts, connections between spot prices, trading pairs, and the derivatives markets are coming into focus.\par \par \uc2 Liquidations And Profit-Taking\par \par \uc2 With Bitcoin (BTC) facing significant selling pressure, its market dominance dropped to $57% as liquidations amplified its downward trajectory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe asset dipped to an intraday low of $92,600 before rebounding as spot ETFs registered $500 million in outflows, signaling potential profit taking. BTC may experience \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short-term as $9.4 billion worth of options expire on Friday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several other cryptocurrencies, including Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ), Ripple (XRP), Dogecoin (DOGE), Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), and Tron (TRX), also registered substantial declines.\par \par \uc2 Trump Plans To Hand Over Crypto Oversight to CFTC\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump is reportedly mulling handing oversight of the crypto industry to the \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  (CFTC) in a move that could significantly roll back regulatory control from the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC). The move would allow the CFTC to regulate spot markets for digital assets deemed commodities. Trump believes the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s enforcement action against the crypto space has adversely impacted crypto innovation in the US, and a less stringent approach could facilitate more growth. If the CFTC is given regulatory control over crypto, it would be a big win for the crypto industry, which has long batted for a fairer approach. Former CFTC Chairman \uc2 Chris Giancarlo\uc2  stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith adequate funding and under the right leadership, I think the CFTC could hit the ground running to begin regulating digital commodities on day one of Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/BTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) }}}\uc2  plummeted below the $92,000 support level, falling to an intraday low of $90,707 on Wednesday as a market correction drove prices lower. The retreat from the $100,000 price level can be attributed to profit-booking and investors hoping for a de-escalation in Middle East tensions, which has seen prices of safe-haven assets such as BTC drop. According to \uc2 Mati Greenspan\uc2 , founder and CEO of Quantum Economics, a brief pullback is expected before the next rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin has been on an absolute tear since Election Day, with very few pullbacks. However, the $100,000 level remains a formidable psychological barrier. While breaking through now would be a major \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  signal, a brief pullback may be needed to gather momentum before the next attempt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Bitcoin price chart shows a significant correction at the beginning of the week as the price retreats further from the crucial $100,000 level. BTC has been on an absolute tear since the elections, meeting expectations of surging past the $90,000 level. Analysts expect the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency to cross the $100,000 mark sooner rather than later. BTC went above $90,000 last Monday, increasing 1.17%. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted as BTC rose to $92,457 on Tuesday and $94,204 on Wednesday as markets continued to push higher. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Thursday as BTC surged past $95,000 after an increase of almost 4% and settled at $97,784. BTC set a new all-time high on Friday as it went above $99,000 for the first time, peaking at $99,655 before declining to $98,355.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/0AstO7eC/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView }}}\par \par \uc2 The weekend saw an uptick in selling pressure as BTC encountered resistance around the $100,000 level. As a result, the price dropped by 1.26% to $97,113. Sellers drove BTC to an intraday low of $94,838 as selling pressure persisted. However, it recovered from this level to register an increase of 0.80% and settled at $97,891. The current week began with BTC experiencing a significant decline of just over 5% as it plummeted to $92,845. Buyers attempted a recovery on Tuesday as BTC rose to a day high of $95,012. However, buyers lost momentum at this level and BTC plummeted to a low of $90,707 before settling at $91,913. The current session sees BTC up by 1.40% as buyers attempt to mount a recovery despite facing growing selling pressure.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts expected a market correction as BTC neared $100,000, with indicators like the \uc2 RSI\uc2  showing BTC firmly in the overbought territory. However, whether the correction drags BTC below $90,000 remains to be seen. Market watchers anticipated a correction but are confident BTC will break above the $100,000 barrier by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, when new all-time highs are reached, there is typically a period of consolidation before further moves up. We know that new institutional money is coming into the space and retail activity is picking up via ETFs and exchanges. With positive macro and regulatory news ahead, we could see an uptick in price activity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ETH-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) }}}\uc2  rebounded impressively to stay above $3,000 as buyers looked for a way past the resistance at $3,500 and move towards $4000. Despite starting the previous week on a positive note, ETH fell back on Tuesday, dropping over 3% to $3,110. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted on Wednesday as ETH dropped by 1.26% to $3,070. However, ETH made a strong recovery on Thursday, surging by 9.42% and settling at $3,360, going above the crucial $3,300 price level. ETH experienced significant \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday as buyers attempted a move higher and sellers looked to drag ETH lower. Sellers ultimately gained the upper hand, and ETH fell by 0.96% to $3,328. Buyers returned to the market on Saturday as ETH surged to a high of $3,502 before declining and settling at $3,396, an increase of just over 2%.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/cjnoHwUQ/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView }}}\par \par \uc2 Sunday saw an increase in selling pressure as ETH dropped to an intraday low of $3,288. However, it recovered from this level to settle at $3,301, registering a decline of 1.01%. The current week began with ETH surging past $3,500 and reaching an intraday high of $3,547, but buyers lost momentum after reaching this level and fell back to $3,415. Selling pressure and \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  returned on Tuesday as the price dropped 2.63% to a low of $3,253 before settling at $3,326. The current session sees ETH back in positive territory, with the price up just over 3% and trading at $3,425.\par \par \uc2 Buyers will look to build momentum and push ETH above $3,500. A break above this level could open the doors for a move towards $3,800 or $4,000. On the other hand, if sellers drive ETH below $3,000, the price could drop to $2,850 before recovering.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ) is attempting a recovery as it looks to rebound from the 20-day SMA and push towards $250-$260. The Ethereum killer encountered significant \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past few sessions as prices rose and dipped significantly. \uc2 SOL\uc2  reached $239 last Monday after registering an increase of 1.04%. However, it fell back on Tuesday after a significant uptick in selling pressure and \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highligh